Only define the wcscpy_s / wcscat_s compatibility macros for genuinely old MSVC.

UPSTREAM BUG, and not a clang or a MinGW concern: the guard is written as a bare comparison,
so a compiler that does not define _MSC_VER at all satisfies it. The preprocessor evaluates the
undefined identifier as 0, and 0 is less than 1400, which is how GCC and clang on MinGW end up
taking a code path meant for Visual Studio 2003.

Intel's dispatcher then defines a macro named wcscpy_s, expanding to TWO statements, one of them
a cast of the size argument to void. mfx_dispatcher.h pulls that header in before the .cpp
includes <windows.h>, so the macro is live when windows.h reaches stralign.h. Any use of
wcscpy_s there as a value-returning expression is then a syntax error:

    stralign.h:208:67: error: expected ')'
    stralign.h:208:67: error: cannot initialize return object of type 'PUWSTR'
                              with an rvalue of type 'void'
    stralign.h:208:150: error: extraneous ')' before ';'
      note: expanded from macro 'wcscpy_s'

Two translation units fail this way, mfx_dispatcher.cpp and mfx_load_dll.cpp, taking the whole
qsv plugin and therefore Intel Quick Sync with them.

The macros are unnecessary as well as harmful: mingw-w64 declares the real wcscpy_s in
sec_api/wchar_s.h, and every call site in libmfx uses the count-based signature it expects --
verified by compiling all four call shapes against the real function with the macros absent.
There is no behavioural risk either, because MSVC 2005 and later report 1400 or above, so every
modern Visual Studio build already compiles this code against the real CRT function.

Whether it bites depends on the mingw-w64 headers rather than on the compiler. In one snapshot
the offending helper sits in sec_api/stralign_s.h behind a legacy _WConst_Return guard and is
never compiled; in a newer one it lives in stralign.h itself with nothing gating it. Same clang,
same feature set, one machine builds and the other does not. Worth sending upstream.

--- a/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/qsv/libmfx/dispatcher/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
+++ b/subprojects/gst-plugins-bad/sys/qsv/libmfx/dispatcher/windows/mfx_dispatcher_defs.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #define MAX_PLUGIN_PATH 4096
 #define MAX_PLUGIN_NAME 4096
 
-#if _MSC_VER < 1400
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1400
     #define wcscpy_s(to, to_size, from) \
         (void)(to_size);                \
         wcscpy(to, from)
